  "clause_evidence": {
    "u6-req-0082": "The published dedicated SessionTarget type accepts URI references only in invitation selectors; ordinary routing/resource IDs retain their alphabet and128-byte bound. Current fixed-schema vectors and shared typed decoder agree. Both algorithms exercise actual native and HTTP Session commands preserving original from/to/medium/intent/capability intent, actual configured tel/sip routing, mixed start and duplex; current invitation regressions retain the six native media alternatives.",
    "u6-req-0083": "Current Participant/Identity references retain their original request digest and resolve to exact current member epochs. tel/sip references require a current configured owner-bound gateway registration and exact verified Endpoint/Device/current Conversation member, current Endpoint/route credentials, tenant and recipient authority. Schema99 freezes Endpoint ID/revision/address/policy with the original source; revocation/address reassignment cannot redirect original replay. Removed/unknown/unconfigured/revoked/duplicate targets refuse, and insertion failure rolls back resolution/source/Session atomically. Actual gateway IO independently rechecks current rights; URI text is never a dial grant."
  },
